values ('bbbb0005-0000-4000-8000-000000000028', 'en', null, 'Criminology', 'Criminology is the scientific study of crime, criminals, criminal behavior, and the systems a society uses to prevent and respond to them. This course surveys how crime is defined and measured, the major theories that try to explain it, the main types of crime, and the workings of the criminal justice system, with a steady emphasis on balanced, evidence-based reasoning. Structure adapted from the Criminology article on Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia (CC BY-SA 4.0).', null, 'foundations', 86, true, 'humanities', '{}')
on conflict (id) do nothing;

